<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Sitawaka</h1><p class="st-meta">1521 CE – 1594 CE · capital Sitawaka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Sinhalese kingdom that led the fight against the Portuguese, reaching its height under Rajasinha I.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1521 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kotte">Kingdom of Kotte</a> was divided after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayabahu-kollaya">Vijayabahu Kollaya</a>, a palace revolt in which three princes killed their father. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayadunne">Mayadunne</a> received Sitawaka, an inland district east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombo">Colombo</a>, and became the bitter rival of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuvanaikabahu-vii-of-kotte">Bhuvanaikabahu VII of Kotte</a>, who relied on Portuguese support.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayadunne">Mayadunne</a> waged almost continuous war on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kotte">Kotte</a> and its Portuguese allies. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasinha-i-of-sitawaka">Rajasinha I</a> conquered most of the west and central highlands, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombo">Colombo</a> in 1587 to 1588 and converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a>, which alienated the Buddhist clergy. The kingdom relied on a large peasant army and control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinnamon">cinnamon</a> lands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasinha-i-of-sitawaka">Rajasinha I</a> died in 1593 the kingdom quickly collapsed; the Portuguese occupied Sitawaka by 1594, and much of its territory went to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-ceylon">Portuguese Ceylon</a> while the hill country passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kandy">Kingdom of Kandy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-sitawaka.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Sitawaka" width="320" height="230"><figcaption>Image: Nishadhi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sitawaka_Kingdom_(1521_-_1594).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1521 CE – 1594 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sitawaka</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mayadunne, Rajasinha I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism, Shaivism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sinhala</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Sri Lanka</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sitawaka, Sitavaka kingdom</dd></dl></aside></div>
